    <bpmn:process id="W_W529" name="W529. POS Void &amp; Refund Tiered Authorization" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Cashier initiates void (pre- or post-tender) or refund at POS
Frequency: Multiple daily per store — estimated 2–5 voids/refunds per store per day
Volume: ~400–1,000 voids/refunds/day chain-wide
Owner: Cashier / Store Manager
Participants: Cashier, Department Supervisor, Assistant Store Manager, Store Manager, Regional Manager (by tier)
Source: workflow W529 — POS Void &amp; Refund Tiered Authorization</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W529_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W529_Lane1" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W529_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W529_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W529_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W529_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W529_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W529_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W529_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W529_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W529_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W529_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W529_Lane3" name="Authorizer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W529_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W529_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W529_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W529_Start5" name="Cashier initiates void (pre- or post-tender) or refund at POS">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W529_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W529_Task6" name="Cashier identifies need for void or refund: customer request, pricing error…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Cashier identifies need for void or refund: customer request, pricing error, wrong item scanned, duplicate scan, post-purchase return; Cashier selects &quot;Void&quot; or &quot;Refund&quot; on POS terminal
Responsible (R): Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W529_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W529_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W529_Task7" name="Tier 1 — Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System determines authorization tier based on void/refund amount: Tier 1 — Department Supervisor: ≤ PHP 5,000 (covers most common voids — wrong item, duplicate scan, minor pricing error); Tier 2 — Assistant Store Manager: &gt; PHP 5,000 and ≤ PHP 20,000; Tier 3 — Store Manager: &gt; PHP 20,000 and ≤ PHP 100,000; Tier 4 — Regional Manager: &gt; PHP 100,000 (rare — large trade account returns, high-value project material returns)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W529_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W529_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W529_Task8" name="System prompts Cashier for void/refund reason code (Wrong Item Scanned /…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: System prompts Cashier for void/refund reason code (Wrong Item Scanned / Duplicate Scan / Pricing Error / Customer Changed Mind / Customer Dissatisfied / Damaged Item / Other); Cashier selects reason code
Responsible (R): Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W529_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W529_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W529_Task9" name="System displays required authorizer name and role on cashier screen (e.g…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: System displays required authorizer name and role on cashier screen (e.g., &quot;Authorization Required: Dept. Supervisor — Maria Santos&quot;); Cashier calls or signals the required authorizer to terminal
Responsible (R): System / Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W529_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W529_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W529_Task10" name="Authorizer arrives at terminal; swipes/scan employee ID badge or enters…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Authorizer arrives at terminal; swipes/scan employee ID badge or enters credentials; system verifies authorizer has required role (Department Supervisor / Asst. Manager / Store Manager / Regional Manager); system displays void/refund details (original transaction, amount, reason code, items) for authorizer review
Responsible (R): Authorizer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W529_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W529_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W529_Task11" name="Authorizer reviews void/refund request: verifies amount is reasonable for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Authorizer reviews void/refund request: verifies amount is reasonable for stated reason, checks for patterns (same cashier repeatedly voiding, same customer returning frequently), confirms item(s) are present for refund (if applicable); Authorizer approves or rejects
Responsible (R): Authorizer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W529_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W529_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W529_Task12" name="If approved: system processes void (reverses inventory, payment, loyalty…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: If approved: system processes void (reverses inventory, payment, loyalty points, promo usage per W5B.10) or refund (processes refund to original tender per W12A.6); system records authorization with: authorizer ID, authorizer role, approval timestamp, void/refund amount, reason code, original transaction reference
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W529_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W529_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W529_Task13" name="If rejected: system cancels void/refund request; Cashier informs customer of…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: If rejected: system cancels void/refund request; Cashier informs customer of denial and alternative options (e.g., exchange instead of refund, escalate to Store Manager if Department Supervisor denied); system logs rejected request with reason
Responsible (R): System / Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W529_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W529_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W529_Task14" name="No available authorizer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: No available authorizer: if required-tier authorizer is not physically available in store (e.g., Store Manager is the only Tier 3 authorizer and is off-site): Cashier can request remote authorization — system sends authorization request to authorizer&#x27;s mobile device (push notification with transaction details); authorizer reviews and approves/rejects on mobile; all remote authorizations are logged with GPS location and timestamp of authorization device
Responsible (R): System / Authorizer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W529_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W529_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W529_Task15" name="Daily: system generates void/refund summary report for Store Manager — count…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Daily: system generates void/refund summary report for Store Manager — count and total value by authorization tier, by reason code, by cashier, by authorizer; Store Manager reviews as part of W522 daily transaction review; Regional Manager receives daily summary of all Tier 4 authorizations (&gt; PHP 100,000)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W529_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W529_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W529_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W529_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W529_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-265 (ensure controlled execution — POS Compliance &amp; Controls (PA-08.3).) | - operational: should flag multiple same-customer voids within a session
Owner: Cashier / Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W529_Assoc18" sourceRef="W529_Annotation17" targetRef="W529_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W529_Flow19" sourceRef="W529_Start5" targetRef="W529_Task6" />
