    <bpmn:process id="W_W530" name="W530. POS High-Value Transaction Documentation &amp; Customer ID" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Transaction total exceeds configurable threshold (default: PHP 50,000)
Frequency: Several per store per day — hardware retail has inherently high basket values (contractors, project buyers); ~1–3 high-value transactions per store per day (the PHP 50K trigger is self-limiting vs the ~PHP 840K/day per-store revenue canon)
Volume: ~200–600 high-value transactions/day chain-wide
Owner: Cashier (processing); Store Manager (oversight)
Participants: Cashier, Customer, Store Manager, Loss Prevention (analytics)
Source: workflow W530 — POS High-Value Transaction Documentation &amp; Customer ID</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W530_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W530_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W530_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W530_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W530_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W530_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W530_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W530_Lane2" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W530_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W530_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W530_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W530_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W530_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W530_Lane4" name="LP Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W530_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W530_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W530_Start6" name="Transaction total exceeds configurable threshold (default: PHP 50,000)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W530_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W530_Task7" name="Transaction total exceeds PHP 50,000 (configurable per store or chain-wide)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Transaction total exceeds PHP 50,000 (configurable per store or chain-wide); system displays &quot;High-Value Transaction — Customer Identification Required&quot; prompt on cashier screen
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W530_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W530_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W530_Task8" name="Customer-facing display shows &quot;Transaction requires ID verification — please…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Customer-facing display shows &quot;Transaction requires ID verification — please have your government ID ready&quot;
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W530_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W530_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W530_Task9" name="Cashier verbally requests customer&#x27;s government-issued photo ID; acceptable ID…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Cashier verbally requests customer&#x27;s government-issued photo ID; acceptable ID types: Philippine driver&#x27;s license, passport, national ID (PhilSys), SSS ID, GSIS ID, COMELEC voter&#x27;s ID, postal ID with photo, PRC ID, PhilHealth ID
Responsible (R): Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W530_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W530_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W530_Task10" name="Cashier selects ID type from dropdown on POS terminal; enters ID number (or…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Cashier selects ID type from dropdown on POS terminal; enters ID number (or scans ID barcode if machine-readable); enters customer full name from ID
Responsible (R): Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W530_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W530_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W530_Task11" name="System records customer identification details against transaction: ID type, ID…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: System records customer identification details against transaction: ID type, ID number (encrypted in audit log, last 4 digits visible), customer name, cashier ID, transaction ID, transaction amount; identification details printed on merchant copy of receipt (not on customer copy for privacy)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W530_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W530_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W530_Task12" name="Transaction proceeds to tender per standard W5B.7; if payment is cash and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Transaction proceeds to tender per standard W5B.7; if payment is cash and amount ≥ PHP 500,000: W519 AML reporting process is triggered in addition to high-value documentation
Responsible (R): Cashier / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Per W5B</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W530_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W530_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W530_Task13" name="For loyalty members: system auto-populates customer name from loyalty record…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: For loyalty members: system auto-populates customer name from loyalty record; Cashier only needs to verify and scan/enter ID — reduces data entry to ~30 sec
Responsible (R): System / Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W530_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W530_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W530_Task14" name="Daily: high-value transaction register included in W522 daily review; Store…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Daily: high-value transaction register included in W522 daily review; Store Manager spot-checks high-value transactions for reasonableness (customer name matches purchase type, e.g., contractor buying construction materials)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Part of W522</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W530_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W530_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W530_Task15" name="Weekly: Loss Prevention reviews high-value transaction register for anomalies…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Weekly: Loss Prevention reviews high-value transaction register for anomalies: same customer name with different IDs, same ID at multiple stores, high-value transactions followed by high-value returns (W12), high-value cash transactions (W519 trigger correlation)
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Director
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W530_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W530_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W530_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W530_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W530_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-265 (ensure controlled execution — POS Compliance &amp; Controls (PA-08.3).) | - operational: must enforce separate receipt formats
Owner: Cashier (processing); Store Manager (oversight)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
