    <bpmn:process id="W_W531" name="W531. POS Bagging, Carry-Out &amp; Bag Fee Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Transaction completed; customer requires bags or carry-out assistance for purchased items
Frequency: Per transaction — nearly all transactions require bagging or carry-out in hardware retail
Volume: ~2.8M transactions/month chain-wide (majority requiring some form of bagging or carry-out)
Owner: Cashier (bag fee processing); Sales Associate / Utility Staff (carry-out)
Participants: Cashier, Sales Associate, Customer, Store Manager (ordinance compliance)
Source: workflow W531 — POS Bagging, Carry-Out &amp; Bag Fee Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W531_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W531_Lane1" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W531_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W531_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W531_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W531_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W531_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W531_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W531_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W531_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W531_Lane3" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W531_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W531_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W531_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W531_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W531_Start6" name="Transaction completed; customer requires bags or carry-out assistance for purchased items">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W531_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W531_Task7" name="After tender completion (W5B.8) and receipt printing (W5B.8), Cashier asks…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: After tender completion (W5B.8) and receipt printing (W5B.8), Cashier asks customer: &quot;Would you like a bag?&quot; and offers bag options: small paper bag (if available), large plastic bag, reusable bag (for purchase), or no bag
Responsible (R): Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W531_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W531_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W531_Task8" name="System automatically determines bag fee applicability based on store location…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System automatically determines bag fee applicability based on store location: system reads store location from terminal ID → matches to LGU jurisdiction in location master (W254) → applies LGU-specific bag fee ordinance (e.g., Makati City: PHP 2/bag; Quezon City: PHP 5/bag for plastic; Pasig: PHP 5/plastic bag; Muntinlupa: plastic bag ban — no plastic bags allowed at all; stores in municipalities without ordinance: no bag fee)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W531_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W531_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W531_Task9" name="If bag fee applies: system adds bag fee line item to transaction (already…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: If bag fee applies: system adds bag fee line item to transaction (already completed — bag fee added as post-tender adjustment OR presented as pre-tender line item before final total); system selects bag fee amount per LGU ordinance and bag type; receipt itemizes bag fee separately (&quot;LGU Plastic Bag Fee: PHP 5.00&quot;)
Responsible (R): System / Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W531_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W531_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W531_Task10" name="If customer brings reusable bag: system applies bag fee waiver (no charge)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: If customer brings reusable bag: system applies bag fee waiver (no charge); some LGUs provide incentive (e.g., PHP 1 discount per reusable bag used) — system applies incentive if configured for store location
Responsible (R): System / Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W531_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W531_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W531_Task11" name="Cashier bags items or customer self-bags; oversized items (lumber, cement bags…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Cashier bags items or customer self-bags; oversized items (lumber, cement bags, large tools, appliances) that cannot fit in bags are staged at bagging area for carry-out
Responsible (R): Cashier / Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W531_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W531_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W531_Task12" name="For bulky/heavy items requiring carry-out: Cashier calls Sales Associate or…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: For bulky/heavy items requiring carry-out: Cashier calls Sales Associate or Utility Staff for carry-out assistance; Staff member assists customer to vehicle loading area (W438 yard dispatch for lumber/building materials) or store exit for smaller bulky items; customer signs or acknowledges receipt of items
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Utility Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W531_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W531_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W531_Task13" name="Bag supply replenishment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Bag supply replenishment: Cashier monitors bag supply at terminal; when supply runs low: Cashier notifies Stock Associate to replenish from backroom bag inventory; bag inventory tracked as non-merchandise supply item per W136 (indirect procurement)
Responsible (R): Cashier / Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min (replenishment)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W531_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W531_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W531_Task14" name="Monthly: Store Manager reviews bag fee revenue and compliance — bag fees…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Monthly: Store Manager reviews bag fee revenue and compliance — bag fees collected vs. expected based on transaction volume per LGU ordinance; identifies stores with low bag fee collection (potential non-compliance with LGU ordinance); bag supply consumption report for W136 procurement planning
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 30 min/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W531_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W531_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W531_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W531_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W531_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-265 (ensure controlled execution — POS Compliance &amp; Controls (PA-08.3).) | - operational: Cashier (bag fee processing); Sales Associate / Utility Staff (carry-out) review and approval gate
Owner: Cashier (bag fee processing); Sales Associate / Utility Staff (carry-out)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W531_Assoc17" sourceRef="W531_Annotation16" targetRef="W531_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W531_Flow18" sourceRef="W531_Start6" targetRef="W531_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W531_Flow19" sourceRef="W531_Task7" targetRef="W531_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W531_Flow20" sourceRef="W531_Task8" targetRef="W531_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W531_Flow21" sourceRef="W531_Task9" targetRef="W531_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W531_Flow22" sourceRef="W531_Task10" targetRef="W531_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W531_Flow23" sourceRef="W531_Task11" targetRef="W531_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W531_Flow24" sourceRef="W531_Task12" targetRef="W531_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W531_Flow25" sourceRef="W531_Task13" targetRef="W531_Task14" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W531_Flow26" sourceRef="W531_Task14" targetRef="W531_End15" />
    </bpmn:process>
