    <bpmn:process id="W_W538" name="W538. POS Real-Time Loss Prevention Exception Monitoring &amp; Alert Response" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: POS system detects anomalous transaction pattern in real-time; LP analyst monitors exception dashboard
Frequency: Continuous — ~500–800 exception alerts/day across 200 stores during operating hours
Volume: Peak: bi-monthly sales events generate 2–3× normal exception volume
Owner: Loss Prevention Manager (enterprise); Store Manager (store-level response)
Participants: LP Analyst (monitoring), Store Manager (response), Cashier (involved in flagged transaction), Regional LP Manager (escalation)
Source: workflow W538 — POS Real-Time Loss Prevention Exception Monitoring &amp; Alert Response</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W538_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W538_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W538_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W538_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W538_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W538_Lane2" name="LP Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W538_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W538_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W538_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W538_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W538_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W538_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W538_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W538_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W538_Start5" name="POS system detects anomalous transaction pattern in real-time; LP analyst monitors…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W538_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W538_Task6" name="Real-time exception detection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Real-time exception detection: LP analytics engine continuously monitors POS event stream (W533) for anomaly patterns: (a) high void rate per cashier (&gt; 5% of transactions in 1-hour window), (b) excessive no-sale drawer opens (&gt; 3 per hour per cashier), (c) rapid consecutive voids (&gt; 2 voids within 5 minutes by same cashier), (d) price override frequency exceeding threshold, (e) sweethearting detection (repeated low-value scans followed by high-value manual entry), (f) pass-through detection (weight mismatch between scanned barcode and expected item weight at SCO), (g) refund/return frequency exceeding threshold per cashier, (h) manual card entry (non-EMV) above baseline, (i) loyalty points gaming patterns
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Real-time (&lt; 30 sec from event)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W538_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W538_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W538_Task7" name="Alert classification and routing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Alert classification and routing: system classifies each detected anomaly by severity: (a) Critical (active fraud suspected — immediate response required): sweethearting, pass-through fraud, serial void-refund pattern; (b) High (suspicious pattern — same-shift response): excessive voids, frequent overrides, coupon stacking abuse; (c) Medium (anomalous but explainable — next-day review): slightly elevated void rate, higher-than-average discount usage; (d) Low (statistical noise — logged for trend analysis); Critical and High alerts pushed to LP Analyst dashboard and Store Manager mobile app in real-time; Medium alerts queued for W522 daily review
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W538_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W538_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W538_Task8" name="Critical alert triage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Critical alert triage: LP Analyst reviews critical alert on dashboard; assesses context (cashier history, transaction details, CCTV snapshot if available, recent performance metrics from W522); determines if active intervention is warranted
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: 3–5 min per alert</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W538_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W538_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W538_Task9" name="Store-level response for Critical alerts">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Store-level response for Critical alerts: LP Analyst contacts Store Manager (or on-duty supervisor) via secure channel with alert details; Store Manager observes cashier covertly; if fraud confirmed, Store Manager intervenes per W37 (LP investigation protocol); if false positive, LP Analyst dismisses alert and notes reason for ML model improvement
Responsible (R): LP Analyst / Store Manager
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: 5–15 min per response</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W538_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W538_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W538_Task10" name="High alert same-shift review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: High alert same-shift review: at next natural break (shift handover W517 or mid-shift), Store Manager reviews High alerts for their cashiers; reviews transaction-level detail; coaches cashier if pattern is procedural error; escalates to LP if pattern appears deliberate
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 min per alert</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W538_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W538_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W538_Task11" name="Medium alert daily review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Medium alert daily review: Medium alerts consolidated into W522 daily transaction review; Store Manager addresses during next-day cashier performance audit
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Per W522</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W538_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W538_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W538_Task12" name="Pattern analytics &amp; model tuning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Pattern analytics &amp; model tuning: LP Analyst reviews weekly exception summary: alert volume by store, severity distribution, false-positive rate, confirmed fraud cases; adjusts detection thresholds; feeds confirmed cases back to ML model for continuous improvement; monthly report to LP Manager
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: ~2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W538_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W538_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W538_Task13" name="Cross-store serial fraud detection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Cross-store serial fraud detection: system detects same customer (loyalty ID, payment card token, or phone number) triggering exceptions across multiple stores within defined period; LP Analyst investigates cross-store pattern; coordinates with affected Store Managers
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W538_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W538_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W538_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W538_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W538_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-265 (ensure controlled execution — POS Compliance &amp; Controls (PA-08.3).) | - operational: severity classification and ML model tuning with confirmed-case feedback; operational: clear LP policy disclosure in cashier onboarding (W518) and union coordination (W493); operational: edge CCTV processing or direct POS-to-camera timestamp correlation
Owner: Loss Prevention Manager (enterprise); Store Manager (store-level response)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W538_Assoc16" sourceRef="W538_Annotation15" targetRef="W538_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
