    <bpmn:process id="W_W605" name="W605. Return Fraud Detection &amp; Serial Returner Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Return transaction processed at POS (W12) or system generates return pattern alert
Frequency: Continuous; ~56,000 returns/month across 200 stores (~2% return rate)
Volume: Fraudulent returns estimated at 3-5% of total returns = ~1,700–2,800/month
Owner: Loss Prevention Officer (LPO)
Participants: LPO, Store Manager, POS Cashier, LP Analyst (HQ), Customer Service Counter staff
Source: workflow W605 — Return Fraud Detection &amp; Serial Returner Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W605_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W605_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W605_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W605_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W605_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W605_Lane2" name="LPO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W605_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W605_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W605_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W605_Lane3" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W605_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W605_Lane4" name="LP Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W605_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W605_Lane5" name="LP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W605_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W605_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W605_Start7" name="Return transaction processed at POS (W12) or system generates return pattern alert">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W605_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W605_Task8" name="System continuously monitors return transactions for fraud indicators: (a) same…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System continuously monitors return transactions for fraud indicators: (a) same customer &gt; 3 returns in 30 days, (b) returns without receipt &gt; 2 in 30 days, (c) high-value returns (&gt; PHP 10,000), (d) return of commonly wardrobed items (power tools, appliances), (e) return at different store than purchase (cross-store returns), (f) receipt appears altered or duplicated
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W605_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W605_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W605_Task9" name="When fraud indicator triggered: system generates alert to LPO dashboard and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: When fraud indicator triggered: system generates alert to LPO dashboard and Store Manager mobile app with alert classification: Yellow (monitoring), Orange (likely fraud), Red (confirmed pattern)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W605_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W605_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W605_Task10" name="Yellow alerts">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Yellow alerts: LPO adds customer to watch list; reviews transaction history; no customer-facing action
Responsible (R): LPO
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W605_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W605_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W605_Task11" name="Orange alerts">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Orange alerts: LPO investigates customer&#x27;s full return history across all 200 stores; reviews CCTV footage of return transaction; checks loyalty account for anomalies; prepares case summary
Responsible (R): LPO
Accountable (A): LP Analyst
Duration: 20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W605_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W605_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W605_Task12" name="Red alerts (confirmed pattern)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Red alerts (confirmed pattern): LPO coordinates with LP Analyst for cross-store pattern analysis; if fraud confirmed: (a) customer flagged in system with return restriction (receipt-only returns, manager override required), (b) if employee collusion suspected, escalates per W248, (c) if organized retail crime, escalates per W490
Responsible (R): LPO
Accountable (A): LP Analyst
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W605_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W605_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W605_Task13" name="Store-level return policy enforcement: for flagged customers, Cashier receives…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Store-level return policy enforcement: for flagged customers, Cashier receives system prompt requiring manager authorization for return; Customer Service Counter staff trained on receipt verification, product condition assessment, and time-since-purchase validation
Responsible (R): Cashier / CS Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min/return</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W605_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W605_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W605_Task14" name="Weekly: LP Analyst generates return fraud analytics report — top serial…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Weekly: LP Analyst generates return fraud analytics report — top serial returners, fraud rate by store, fraud rate by category, common fraud methods, recovery value from fraud prevention
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W605_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W605_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W605_Task15" name="Monthly: LP Manager reviews return policy effectiveness; recommends threshold…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Monthly: LP Manager reviews return policy effectiveness; recommends threshold adjustments to system fraud detection rules; coordinates with Merchandising on high-return-rate SKUs for root cause analysis (quality issues vs. fraud)
Responsible (R): LP Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W605_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W605_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W605_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W605_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W605_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-265 (ensure controlled execution — POS Compliance &amp; Controls (PA-08.3).) | - operational: trade account exemption from standard return frequency thresholds and human review before restrictions; operational: enterprise-wide return history query in real-time; operational: BIR-compliant sequential receipt numbering (W540) and barcode-based receipt validation at POS
Owner: Loss Prevention Officer (LPO)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W605_Assoc18" sourceRef="W605_Annotation17" targetRef="W605_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W605_Flow19" sourceRef="W605_Start7" targetRef="W605_Task8" />
