    <bpmn:process id="W_W1305" name="W1305. Catch-Weight &amp; Variable-Quantity Item POS Pricing Verification &amp; Scale Calibration Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly scale calibration schedule; or customer complaint about weight-based pricing; or BIR/DENR inspection advisory
Frequency: Quarterly calibration per store (200 stores × ~4 scales each = ~800 calibrations/quarter); daily price verification for catch-weight items
Volume: ~800 scales chain-wide (200 stores × 4: lumber yard scale, hardware bulk scale, produce/garden scale, receiving dock scale); ~5,000 catch-weight SKUs (~14% of active SKUs)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Department Supervisor, Maintenance/Utility Staff, Scale Calibration Technician (contracted), POS System Administrator
Source: workflow W1305 — Catch-Weight &amp; Variable-Quantity Item POS Pricing Verification &amp; Scale Calibration Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1305_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1305_Lane1" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1305_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1305_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1305_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1305_Lane2" name="Scale Calibration Technician">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1305_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1305_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1305_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1305_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1305_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1305_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1305_Start6" name="Quarterly scale calibration schedule; or customer complaint about weight-based pricing…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1305_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1305_Task7" name="Daily catch-weight price verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily catch-weight price verification: (a) during opening procedure (W5A), Department Supervisor verifies catch-weight prices at POS: (i) test-weigh a known-weight item (calibration weight) on each store scale — verify displayed weight matches within ± 10g tolerance, (ii) verify price-per-unit for top 20 catch-weight items matches current ERP price: lumber price per board foot, nails price per kg, wire price per meter, (iii) scan catch-weight barcode label from a pre-printed test label — verify POS displays correct item, weight, and price calculation; (b) log verification results in daily checklist; (c) if any discrepancy: (i) price error: report to Store Manager for immediate correction in POS — price update pushed from ERP, (ii) scale inaccuracy: take scale out of service and use backup scale pending calibration
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1305_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1305_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1305_Task8" name="Quarterly professional scale calibration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quarterly professional scale calibration: (a) contracted Scale Calibration Technician visits each store quarterly per maintenance schedule (W47); (b) technician calibrates each scale using NIST-traceable calibration weights: (i) zero-point verification, (ii) linearity test (test at 25%, 50%, 75%, 100% of scale capacity), (iii) repeatability test (same weight weighed 5 times — must be within ± 0.1% of reading); (c) if scale fails calibration: (i) attempt adjustment per manufacturer procedure, (ii) if adjustment fails: scale replaced from spare inventory at regional office, failed scale sent for repair; (d) technician issues calibration certificate per scale with: scale serial number, calibration date, test results, next calibration due date, technician signature and accreditation number; (e) calibration certificate filed in ERP maintenance module and displayed near scale (LGU inspection requirement)
Responsible (R): Scale Calibration Technician
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/store/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1305_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1305_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1305_Task9" name="LGU weights &amp; measures inspection readiness">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: LGU weights &amp; measures inspection readiness: (a) when LGU announces weights and measures inspection: Store Manager ensures: (i) all scales have current calibration certificates displayed, (ii) LGU verification seals (lead wire seal on scale adjustment mechanism) are intact — broken seal indicates potential tampering, (iii) catch-weight price labels are clearly displayed per DTI requirements (price per kg, price per meter, price per board foot), (iv) scale display is visible to customer during weighing (Consumer Act requirement), (v) receipt shows item, weight, unit of measure, price per unit, and total price for catch-weight items; (b) LGU inspector may: (i) test scales with their own calibration weights, (ii) verify price accuracy for catch-weight items, (iii) issue compliance certificate or notice of violation; (c) for violations: Store Manager has 5 days to correct; uncorrected violations result in fines and potential store closure per LGU ordinance
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Per inspection: 2–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1305_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1305_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1305_Task10" name="Catch-weight inventory accuracy reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Catch-weight inventory accuracy reconciliation: Weekly, Department Supervisor reconciles catch-weight inventory: (a) for bulk items (nails, screws by kg): compare POS sales volume (total kg sold per SKU per week) to physical bin inventory change; (b) for lumber: compare POS board foot sales to physical count change; (c) investigate variances &gt; 3%: (i) scale inaccuracy (over- or under-weighing), (ii) measurement rounding at POS, (iii) spillage/waste not recorded, (iv) pilferage; (d) post inventory adjustment per threshold with Store Manager approval
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1305_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1305_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1305_Task11" name="Catch-weight pricing change management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Catch-weight pricing change management: When Category Manager changes catch-weight item prices: (a) system pushes price update to all POS terminals in real-time (continuous sync per POS-013); (b) Department Supervisor receives notification of price change with effective date/time; (c) Supervisor updates shelf/bin price labels for catch-weight items before first customer transaction at new price; (d) system prevents sale of catch-weight item at old price after effective time — auto-rejects if POS cache has stale price; (e) price change log maintained for BIR audit trail (price history per SKU with dates)
Responsible (R): System / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Per price change event: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1305_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1305_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1305_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1305_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1305_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-184 (ensure POS settlement &amp; tender reconciliation completeness.) | - operational: Store Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1305_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1305_Annotation13" targetRef="W1305_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
