    <bpmn:process id="W_W1516" name="W1516. Philippine BIR Electronic Invoicing System (EIS) Sales Data Transmission &amp; Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Each POS sales transaction completion; BIR EIS daily/weekly batch submission deadlines
Frequency: Continuous real-time or near-real-time per transaction; daily batch reconciliation to BIR EIS portal
Volume: ~2.8M POS transactions/month across 200 stores (~467/store/day)
Owner: Tax Compliance Manager
Participants: Tax Compliance Manager, IT POS Team, Finance Controller, Store Department Supervisor
Source: workflow W1516 — Philippine BIR Electronic Invoicing System (EIS) Sales Data Transmission &amp; Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1516_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1516_Lane1" name="Tax Compliance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1516_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1516_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1516_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1516_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1516_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1516_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1516_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1516_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1516_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1516_Start4" name="Each POS sales transaction completion; BIR EIS daily/weekly batch submission deadlines">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1516_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1516_Task5" name="BIR EIS registration and setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: BIR EIS registration and setup: (a) Tax Compliance Manager registers each store location (200 stores + 4 DCs + HQ) with BIR EIS portal; (b) receives unique facility TIN-EIS credentials; (c) IT POS Team configures each POS terminal to generate BIR-compliant sales data fields: (i) seller TIN, (ii) registered name, (iii) store address, (iv) transaction date/time, (v) item description per line, (vi) quantity, (vii) unit price, (viii) VAT amount, (ix) total amount, (x) official receipt/invoice number per BIR sequential format
Responsible (R): Tax Compliance Manager / IT POS Team
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: Initial setup: 2–3 months</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1516_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1516_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1516_Task6" name="Per-transaction data generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Per-transaction data generation: (a) POS system generates electronic sales record for each completed transaction with all BIR-mandated fields; (b) system assigns BIR-compliant sequential OR/SI number; (c) record stored in local queue (for offline resilience) and queued for transmission to BIR EIS; (d) customer receipt printed with BIR-required details including &quot;TIN: xxx-xxx-xxx&quot; header, &quot;VAT Registered&quot; marker, and QR code linking to electronic record
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated per transaction</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1516_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1516_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1516_Task7" name="Data transmission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Data transmission: (a) system transmits queued sales records to BIR EIS via API/SFTP in real-time (preferred) or batch mode (minimum daily); (b) for stores experiencing internet outage: records queued locally and transmitted upon connectivity restoration within 24-hour tolerance window; (c) system logs transmission status: sent, acknowledged, rejected (with rejection reason)
Responsible (R): System / IT POS Team
Accountable (A): Tax Compliance Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1516_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1516_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1516_Task8" name="Daily reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Daily reconciliation: (a) Tax Compliance Manager or designee runs daily EIS reconciliation report: (i) total transactions in POS system vs. total records transmitted to BIR EIS, (ii) records acknowledged by BIR vs. pending/rejected, (iii) sequential OR number gap analysis (no missing OR numbers per BIR requirement); (b) for rejected records: IT POS Team investigates rejection reason (format error, missing field, duplicate OR number), corrects, and retransmits; (c) for transmission gaps (offline stores): verify all records queued during outage were transmitted upon reconnection
Responsible (R): Tax Compliance Manager / IT POS Team
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 30–60 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1516_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1516_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1516_Task9" name="Monthly compliance certification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly compliance certification: (a) Tax Compliance Manager generates monthly EIS compliance report: (i) total transactions submitted vs. total POS transactions (target: 100%), (ii) rejection rate (target: &lt; 0.1%), (iii) average transmission latency (target: &lt; 4 hours), (iv) sequential OR number integrity confirmation; (b) Finance Controller reviews and signs off; (c) report filed for BIR audit readiness (10-year retention per A6.5)
Responsible (R): Tax Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1516_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1516_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1516_Task10" name="BIR audit response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: BIR audit response: when BIR selects BuildRight for EIS compliance audit: (a) Tax Compliance Manager extracts requested transaction samples from system; (b) provides transmission logs, acknowledgment receipts, and sequential OR number continuity evidence; (c) coordinates with external tax counsel if BIR raises deficiencies
Responsible (R): Tax Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Per audit event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1516_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1516_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1516_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1516_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1516_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-265 (ensure controlled execution — POS Compliance &amp; Controls (PA-08.3).) | - operational: Tax Compliance Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Tax Compliance Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
